<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended April 9, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Apr 9  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.92   -0.193    +0.577</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     8.60   -2.678    +1.962</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	463.66   -2.645    +4.016</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 132.80   -2.600   -30.700</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.85   -0.044    +2.136</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.59	68.71	58.48</p>
<p>M2					 392.19     394.81     386.93</p>
<p>M3					 499.91     497.81     473.39</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Feb	   Jan</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-19.81	-16.27</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     692.64	685.17</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.81	105.23</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
